  "comments": {
    "overrides": "Transitive-only security pins. fast-uri comes from the Prisma CLI tree and exists so we can patch it without downgrading Prisma 7 to 6. Re-check on each Prisma upgrade and drop any entry Prisma has caught up with: as of Prisma 7.10.1 its own pins of mysql2/deepmerge-ts/valibot are the patched versions and hono/@hono/node-server are no longer in the tree, so those entries were dropped. fast-uri is forced to v4 although ajv (via @prisma/streams-local) still declares ^3; v4's only runtime change is an escaping fix and ajv's parse/resolve/serialize usage is unaffected. postcss follows the direct devDependency ($postcss) so Next.js's own exact pin is lifted with it. sharp is pinned for Next.js's image optimizer (librsvg CVE)."
  },
  "overrides": {
    "lodash": ">=4.17.24",
    "postcss": "$postcss",
    "nanoid": "^3.3.18",
    "sharp": "^0.35.5",
    "fast-uri": "^4.2.3"
  }
}
